        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in nanoid. Affected versions of nanoid mishandles non-integer values. When nanoid is called with a fractional value, there were a number of undesirable effects:\n\n- In browser and non-secure, the code infinite loops on while (size--)\n- In node, the value of poolOffset becomes fractional, causing calls to nanoid to return zeroes until the pool is next filled: when i is initialized to poolOffset, pool[i] & 63 -> undefined & 63 -> 0\n- If the first call in node is a fractional argument, the initial buffer allocation fails with an error\n\nThe highest impact of this issue system availability.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
